# Industrial 4–20 mA Signal Conditioning & Analog Fault Detection

## Overview

Design and simulation of an industrial analog current-loop system using LTspice.

## System Architecture

0–5 V Sensor
→ Buffer
→ Low-Pass Filter
→ Command Voltage Generation
→ Closed-Loop Current Transmitter
→ 24 V Current Loop
→ 250 Ω Receiver
→ 1–5 V
→ Analog Fault Detection

## Specifications

| Parameter | Value |
|---|---:|
| Sensor input | 0–5 V |
| Loop current | 4–20 mA |
| Supply | 24 V DC |
| Receiver resistance | 250 Ω |
| Receiver output | 1–5 V |
| Filter cutoff | 15.9 Hz |
| Low-current threshold | 3.6 mA |
| Over-current threshold | >20 mA |

## Transfer Function

I_loop = 4 mA + 3.2 mA/V × V_in

## Main Features

- Analog signal conditioning
- 10 kΩ / 1 µF low-pass filter
- Closed-loop current regulation
- 24 V industrial current loop
- 250 Ω current-to-voltage conversion
- Analog low/open-loop detection
- Analog over-current detection
- LTspice simulation

## Simulation

### DC Sweep

